<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Breaking news from AFRICA, Maghreb and Sub-Saharan Africa - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of events, politics and social issues across Africa, including North Africa (the Maghreb) and the Sahel, aided by our network of correspondents and experts across the continent.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:47Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nigeria records first Ebola case as outbreak spreads across Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4bc5f86de7474612e0e31f76514e3b034410bb1c5ec831ba8d4a0291ecc3bd7b</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T23:18:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-nigeria-records-first-ebola-case-as-outbreak-spreads-across-africa--ff482f120a86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-nigeria-records-first-ebola-case-as-outbreak-spreads-across-africa" /><summary type="html">Nigeria has confirmed its first Ebola case in Africa's latest outbreak, while Kenya reported its ninth infection, raising fears of further spread across the continent. Africa CDC chief Jean Kaseya warned of an “extremely serious threat” and urged the international community to send funding, medical supplies and health workers.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria confirms first Ebola case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:204dc83aecdd7286b8ca3316cde930067c7a33f1263748c2a22b412f725fc217</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:02:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T21:28:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nigeria-confirms-first-ebola-case--b377a3f657f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nigeria-confirms-first-ebola-case" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, Nigeria confirms its first Ebola case in the midst of an outbreak that began in DRC Congo in mid-May. Also, a former top South African police officer facing sexual grooming and rape charges is denied bail. Finally, São Tomé and Príncipe's rich volcanic soils produce vanilla pods with an entrancing taste unlike those grown anywhere else.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>More than 150 killed in Sudan drone strike on disputed Abyei border region</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ab4f71a52fde8fc05904124bd759491ac4971da4975a1fc1308c67d30674100</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T16:24:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-more-than-150-killed-sudan-drone-strike-disputed-abyei-border-region--03bda77246f1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261020-more-than-150-killed-sudan-drone-strike-disputed-abyei-border-region" /><summary type="html">At least 153 people have been killed in a drone strike on a market in the disputed Abyei region, where a fire at a nearby fuel depot continued to burn on Tuesday. Local officials blamed Sudan’s military for Monday’s attack, which also left dozens injured.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ivorian DJ digs forgotten tracks, on the hunt for great classics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49fe5c65838f71f02a4075d901e2bff98468d7fc3ab608f01650da776b9f0ff9</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T13:09:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-ivorian-dj-digs-forgotten-tracks-on-the-hunt-for-great-classics--6c4fe973b0a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-ivorian-dj-digs-forgotten-tracks-on-the-hunt-for-great-classics" /><summary type="html">Cédric Kouamé travels across Ivory Coast to collect old vinyl records before restoring them. The Ivorian DJ hopes to bring national attention to his passion through an official centre dedicated to the country's historical archives, as FRANCE 24's team on the ground reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Exiled critic of Rwandan President Kagame found beheaded in Uganda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bd83333ff7cdb8d9b627304aa81f206ff1600d80bc1d60fa94723edc96de317</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:34:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-exiled-critic-of-rwandan-president-kagame-found-beheaded-in-uganda--41f173b50df6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-exiled-critic-of-rwandan-president-kagame-found-beheaded-in-uganda" /><summary type="html">Robert Kabera, a former Rwandan soldier living in Uganda, where he had become a vocal critic of his government back home, was found decapitated near Kampala. Rwandan authorities have been accused of assassinating opponents of President Paul Kagame. FRANCE 24's Aurore Bayoud reports from Kigali, Rwanda.</summary></entry><entry><title>Niger, Mali and Burkina Faso resume dialogue with ECOWAS regional bloc</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a898134decf864717643d767092180b98728599ab0fa0b4aaf8a09526f11d5c</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:21:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-niger-mali-and-burkina-faso-resume-dialogue-with-ecowas-regional-bloc--45a34bb01829.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-niger-mali-and-burkina-faso-resume-dialogue-with-ecowas-regional-bloc" /><summary type="html">Three junta-ruled Sahel states – Niger, Mali and Burkina Faso – on Saturday resumed dialogue with the ECOWAS regional bloc, which they withdrew from more than 18 months ago. They agreed to work towards a “framework agreement” on cooperation. FRANCE 24’s regional correspondent Harold Girard tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kenyan cult leader found guilty of murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ada51ac76ce99ed7d2141cb9ef91a88500fc1874b7b5607343cad3f48a771796</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:15:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261020-kenyan-cult-leader-found-guilty-of-murder--a2020938a17e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261020-kenyan-cult-leader-found-guilty-of-murder" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: Kenyan cult leader Paul Mackenzie is convicted of 191 murders, 190 of which were of children. Also, a former Rwandan soldier and outspoken government critic, Robert Kabera, is found decapitated in Uganda. Plus we meet a young Ivorian music lover who travels around the country looking for old-school sounds that need a little TLC.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Drone attacks kill scores in Sudan's West Kordofan state and capital Khartoum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb9561bc97a57babb46daada0596779e0dde11e3ab421c1d4682e7ee32b06815</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:00:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261019-drone-attack-near-southern-sudan-market-kills-scores--3bb8acb831d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261019-drone-attack-near-southern-sudan-market-kills-scores" /><summary type="html">At least 80 people were killed in a drone strike near a market in Sudan’s southern West Kordofan state, a medical source and a witness said Monday, in one of the deadliest single attacks since the Sudan war erupted in 2023. A separate drone attack Monday in the capital Khartoum killed four, including three children.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya confirms third Ebola case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d6b1d44ee8eceefbb75d404c7caa8d48c22c6fbdf01acbf91d3d57363979643</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T20:25:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenya-confirms-third-ebola-case--716df01d45d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-confirms-third-ebola-case" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: Kenya confirms a third case of Ebola, a relative of a man who died earlier this month after travelling from DR Congo. Also, Cameroonian journalist Ambe Macmillan is recovering in hospital after being shot in the legs by gunmen in Bamenda. Finally, we meet Ghanaian artist Ibrahim Mahama, who digs deep into his country's colonial and industrial past to lay new creative foundations for generations to come.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia announces interim government in Tigray, aims for polls in six months</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:487ed843024ce1879d9ee491491c494674cd06b89b86186e7a26dec42f756eb5</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T13:05:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261016-ethiopia-announces-interim-government-tigray-calls-for-polls-six-months--700df3aad3df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261016-ethiopia-announces-interim-government-tigray-calls-for-polls-six-months" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed on Friday announced the appointment of an interim administration to prepare elections in the northern Tigray region previously controlled by the Tigray People's Liberation Front that has clashed with government forces since September. The recent conflict revived a war that killed hundreds of thousands between 2020 and 2022.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Kinshasa braces for potential conflict as Kabila joins M23</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f89aa7457342afd4437ed16d9bcea5ae138ec87d0d5b9bcde0f3eec03df8b196</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T20:29:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kinshasa-braces-for-potential-conflict-as-kabila-joins-m23--7a7b7a23cc35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kinshasa-braces-for-potential-conflict-as-kabila-joins-m23" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: As former Congolese president Joseph Kabila returns to centre stage with a new alliance with the M23 rebels, political leaders in DR Congo are having to choose sides. Also, the US is calling for restraint in Ethiopia as a rights group warns that the conflict in Tigray is already taking a toll on civilians. And as the season of art fairs returns, we take a look at the rising international visibility of African contemporary art.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports second Ebola case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d7e4433c0af82c2e71c8e2bf00f4c19b9c34643318c456f6a01f3266f3cc3d98</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenya-reports-second-ebola-case--4bbcfe9280cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-reports-second-ebola-case" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Kenya confirms a second case of Ebola. Also, Nobel Peace Prize winner Navi Pillay warns that international justice is facing growing pressure. Plus millions of people in Nigeria have been without TikTok for about a month.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo's Kabila launches new coalition with M23</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:587d1678b2ae203d06a715eace8fb45cdee95db05c1c7d0a5439b041f6ff9503</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:21:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kabila-launches-new-coalition-with-m23--ed60166777a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kabila-launches-new-coalition-with-m23" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: DR Congo's former president Joseph Kabila has been named leader of a new rebel coalition, vowing to topple the Congolese government. Also, Africa's largest ever IPO has been extended. Plus Formula ⁠1 ⁠will return to ⁠Africa in ​the early 2030s, once a new circuit is built in Rwanda.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>In Kenya, recycled plastic gets a second life as chess pieces</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9b314f10a719465175407b02e260e801a0925eba152efa945797be8b3b34b73</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:28:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/in-kenya-recycled-plastic-gets-a-second-life-as-chess-pieces--70350efdf983.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/in-kenya-recycled-plastic-gets-a-second-life-as-chess-pieces" /><summary type="html">In Nairobi, a project is helping children develop focus, patience and critical thinking through chess, using pieces made from recycled plastic waste.</summary></entry><entry><title>South Africa suspends asylum applications amid renewed anti-immigrant protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b11503837c4748cc6a105af2aecb385f4e5ba95ea293b5fcf1e90db4195bc42b</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:15:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-amid-renewed-anti-immigrant-protests--0599fa64feef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-amid-renewed-anti-immigrant-protests" /><summary type="html">Tensions have flared in South Africa after a court ruling prompted the government to open its application system to all foreign nationals, regardless of their legal status. Despite applications remaining subject to approval, anti-immigrant protests erupted outside several Home Affairs offices, forcing authorities to temporarily suspend refugee and asylum applications. FRANCE 24's Eunice Masson has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian forces enter key Tigray town, raising fears among residents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0541092e325bfbc3bb16c3242091cb0c4c455ea8a61a7ee208a975575b1e67df</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:13:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-raising-fears-among-residents--da75969b90c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-raising-fears-among-residents" /><summary type="html">Ethiopian federal forces and their allies have entered a key town in northern Tigray near the Eritrean border after rebel fighters withdrew. As the conflict intensifies, residents fear further violence and instability. Tom Canetti has the latest from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Social media becomes a battleground for propaganda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b405ddfde06e35018e596a6a30109038e5e62ce04086b34e9ea881cce6e137f2</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T10:00:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-social-media-becomes-a-battleground-for-propaganda--7bc0eed62661.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-social-media-becomes-a-battleground-for-propaganda" /><summary type="html">Millions of Ethiopians rely on social media for daily news. But as fighting resumes in the country’s north between federal forces and a coalition of rebel groups, these platforms have become a breeding ground for propaganda and disinformation. Pro-government and pro-rebel accounts are battling to shape the news, while journalists’ limited access to the front lines makes it increasingly difficult to verify what is happening on the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tunisian duo Jathb blends Sufi traditions with electronic music</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd0c9a3af1abd79d35fa660038f1100659b9115c578b733a0b599411c1439f68</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T09:59:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tunisian-duo-jathb-blends-sufi-traditions-with-electronic-music--06b68a7b515e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tunisian-duo-jathb-blends-sufi-traditions-with-electronic-music" /><summary type="html">Tunisian musical duo Jathb is reviving traditional Sufi chants by blending them with electronic beats and therapeutic sounds. After four years of gaining recognition both in Tunisia and internationally, the duo is also working to preserve the centuries-old Sufi music and texts that form part of the country’s cultural heritage.</summary></entry><entry><title>DR Congo’s former president Kabila to lead new movement with M23 rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c626a2e7bc11eb684b9ed86c54bd9b7f6d589f477f18a3dbfbe37eefb67218b4</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T21:27:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-dr-congo-former-president-joseph-kabila-to-lead-new-movement-with-m23-rebels--d5bb01da2cbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-dr-congo-former-president-joseph-kabila-to-lead-new-movement-with-m23-rebels" /><summary type="html">Former DR Congo president Joseph Kabila announced a new political-military alliance with Rwanda-backed M23 rebels on Monday, despite being sentenced to death in absentia for alleged complicity with the group. The move comes as debate grows over constitutional changes ahead of President Felix Tshisekedi’s final term ending in 2028.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopian government forces enter key Tigray town near Eritrea border</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71902af3017a53c58920b69fe3eb8249db265ce86a6def0705d11d2da93a24e0</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:34:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-govt-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-near-eritrea-border--b8ceaad00564.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopian-govt-forces-enter-key-tigray-town-near-eritrea-border" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Ethiopian forces tighten their grip on Tigray, advancing into the key town of Adwa after rebels withdrew. Also, police arrest 30 people amid violence across South Africa. Plus we head to Tunisia, where ancient Sufi chants collide with pulsating electronic beats.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>At least 139 migrants die in boat wreck between Djibouti and Yemen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94f3e030076d631ad949b4f1a160a2f5c345ffbd406613050ef2654e90af3248</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:24:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/at-least-139-migrants-die-in-boat-wreck-between-djibouti-and-yemen--b289888d8821.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/at-least-139-migrants-die-in-boat-wreck-between-djibouti-and-yemen" /><summary type="html">At least 139 migrants died, including 15 children and 84 went missing when an overcrowded boat sank on its way from Djibouti to Yemen on the night between October 8 and 9. The International Organization for Migration said most of the people were Ethiopian when the vessel capsized off north of the town of Obock. Details by Morgan Ayre.</summary></entry><entry><title>Scores of gold miners killed in air strikes on Egypt-Sudan border, rights group says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:95980ca26a969995e3a6e643da8bd370ea3a15a757cbeaf8beefd1bc12e84537</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T01:28:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-egypt-sudan-border-airstrikes-gold-miners-killed--da77bc6ac540.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261012-egypt-sudan-border-airstrikes-gold-miners-killed" /><summary type="html">At least 72 workers were killed in air strikes on a gold mine on the Sudan-Egypt border on Saturday, a Sudanese rights group said on Sunday. The Emergency Lawyers organisation accused Egypt’s air force of the attack. AFP could not independently verify the account and Egypt has issued no official comment.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>At least 139 migrants dead, more than 84 missing after boat capsizes off Djibouti</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b62fa0bce66971a96b0702caa92ed3df040487db33d4420cd6e1cf8be9905cd</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-11T09:24:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261011-at-least-hundred-migrants-dead-scores-missing-after-boat-capsizes-off-djibouti--63d1cd578d0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261011-at-least-hundred-migrants-dead-scores-missing-after-boat-capsizes-off-djibouti" /><summary type="html">At least 139 migrants, including at least 15 children, died and 84 remain missing after a boat carrying 350 people capsized off Djibouti en route to Yemen, the International Organisation for Migration said on Sunday.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>South African judge Navi Pillay awarded Nobel Peace Prize</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55b79859e112c8adc8f3bae6ea5cace5f78c8c9fe1f74c17a46af217ba5bddf7</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T21:53:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/south-african-judge-awarded-nobel-peace-prize--abdd3a99d080.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/south-african-judge-awarded-nobel-peace-prize" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme: South African judge and human rights champion Navi Pillay has been awarded the Nobel Peace Prize. Also, in Kenya, health officials in Nairobi are still racing to track dozens of people linked to the man who died from Ebola earlier this week. Finally, Moroccan-British photographer Hassan Hajjaj has built a global reputation with his vibrant portraits, and 40 of his iconic "Rock Stars" are currently taking centre stage in Paris.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Sierra Leone: From 'blood diamonds' to stones of hope?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c18fb58e442e36f389b64c529efd388723f06f81a348b82f66884e6e1f13a9df</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:58:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261009-sierra-leone-from-blood-diamonds-to-stones-of-hopen--522d29c385dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/revisited/20261009-sierra-leone-from-blood-diamonds-to-stones-of-hopen" /><summary type="html">"Blood diamonds" became infamous for funding the brutal civil war in Sierra Leone. Beginning 25 years ago, the Kimberley Process aimed to put an end to this illegal trade. Accused of complicity in the conflict, the diamond industry has since sought to clean up its image, emphasising an ethical shift. But a quarter of a century on, have the former "blood diamonds" truly become synonymous with development? FRANCE 24's Sarah Sakho, Simon Martin and Saidu Bah report.</summary><category term="Revisited" /></entry><entry><title>Foreign aid to Africa falls by over 25%: How women and children are bearing the brunt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40f988a63c93b2c6732e4c0048334aed9c228f98f6211b5ba083d24486da9f3a</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T12:22:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261009-foreign-aid-to-africa-falls-by-over-25-how-women-and-children-are-bearing-the-brunt--1838f18aba87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261009-foreign-aid-to-africa-falls-by-over-25-how-women-and-children-are-bearing-the-brunt" /><summary type="html">As international aid to Africa dries up, what does it mean for women and children on the ground? We report from Kenya on the impact of cuts to US-aid backed health programmes for women. Annette Young also talks to Nana Zulu from the African Women's Development Fund on what it means for the region as a whole. Plus the bravery of Borneo's female firefighters; as Indonesia endures its worst fire season in 11 years, these women are also facing a sexist backlash.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>Eritrea and Ethiopia accuse each other of provoking war as Tigray rebels retreat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:788b3a4ee5a3dbd94fb79b8be1f2c3357c1d44ae65ef258bf018bd63b8338487</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:36:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261009-eritrea-ethiopia-accuse-each-other-of-provoking-war-as-tigray-rebels-retreat--2e14bf93030c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261009-eritrea-ethiopia-accuse-each-other-of-provoking-war-as-tigray-rebels-retreat" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia and Eritrea on Friday accused each other of starting a "war of agresson" days after the two countries severed diplomatic ties. Ethiopian officals estimate that up to 8,000 Eritrean soldiers are present in Tigray supporting rebels who last month launched attacks against federal forces.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Court of Arbitration for Sport hears Senegal's appeal over AFCON title</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25cf525af1d64901213e505c68a1d6e73f9c4f4607d518c45218d560e7c345fa</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T10:48:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261009-court-of-arbitration-for-sport-hears-senegal-s-appeal-over-afcon-title--d066765ef694.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261009-court-of-arbitration-for-sport-hears-senegal-s-appeal-over-afcon-title" /><summary type="html">Ten months after the explosive AFCON final, Senegal and Morocco are still fighting over the title, this time at sport's highest court. A verdict on Senegal's appeal against Morocco's victory by default is expected within days. Also, it's a race against time in Kenya. Health officials are tracing dozens of contacts after an Ebola patient died following a journey from DR Congo. Plus Zimbabwean author Simbarashe Steyn Kundizeza wins the 2026 Caine Prize for African Writing for his short story "The Blue Fighter".</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal and Morocco set for AFCON title rematch – in Swiss sports court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f08d32326d133b3517b7bc2d20afda5fae2b6500e3230bcccc0ec1e2dd486964</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T07:17:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa/20261008-senegal-and-morocco-set-for-afcon-title-rematch-_-swiss-sports-court--c97e824c88b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261008-senegal-and-morocco-set-for-afcon-title-rematch-%E2%80%93-swiss-sports-court" /><summary type="html">Senegal and Morocco on Thursday are again set to fight for the African Cup of Nations title – this time, in the Court of Arbitration for Sport in Switzerland. The closed-door hearing comes nine months after the Confederation of African Football stripped Senegal of their trophy after the team's players walked off the pitch to protest a penalty during the chaotic final roughly nine months ago.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Africa joins the data centre backlash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2d8165488f9a9480169de783f538dff2ebbb430eae90bb3258dfe49057220f3</id><updated>2026-10-21T05:01:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T20:37:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/africa-joins-the-data-center-backlash--51a3f7ecc1aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/africa-joins-the-data-center-backlash" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition: Witnesses say Eritrean troops have moved into Ethiopia's Tigray region, but Asmara rejects the reports. Also, the African Union launches the Africa Credit Rating Agency, aiming to assess the financial health of African states and companies. Plus South African civil society is pushing back against the expansion of data centres that require vast amounts of electricity, water and land.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry></feed>
